rrents in rabbit portal vein myocytes</article-title><source>Am J Physiol</source><year>1992</year><volume>263</volume><fpage>H453</fpage><lpage>H463</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1380775</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>D'Angelo</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Mogford</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Davis</surname><given-names>GE</given-names></name><name><surname>Davis</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Meininger</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Integrin-mediated reduction in vascular smooth muscle [Ca<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup>]<sub>i</sub>induced by RGD-containing peptide</article-title><source>Am J Physiol</source><year>1997</year><volume>272</volume><fpage>H2065</fpage><lpage>H2070</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9139994</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Davis</surname><given-names>GE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Affinity of integrins for damaged extracellular matrix: &#x003b1;<sub>v</sub>&#x003b2;<sub>3</sub>binds to denatured collagen type I through RGD sites</article-title><source>Biochem Biophys  Res Commun</source><year>1992</year><volume>182</volume><fpage>1025</fpage><lpage>1031</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1540151</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dolphin</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Voltage-dependent calcium channels and their modulation by neurotransmitters and G proteins</article-title><source>Exp Physiol</source><year>1995</year><volume>80</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>36</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7734129</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fleischmann</surname><given-names>BK</given-names></name><name><surname>Murray</surname><given-names>RK</given-names></name><name><surname>Kotlikoff</surname><given-names>MI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Voltage window for sustained elevation of cytosolic calcium in smooth muscle cells</article-title><source>Proc Natl  Acad Sci USA</source><year>1994</year><volume>91</volume><fpage>11914</fpage><lpage>11918</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7527547</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ganitkevich</surname><given-names>VY</given-names></name><name><surname>Isenberg</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Depolarization-mediated intracellular calcium transients in isolated smooth muscle cells of guinea-pig urinary bladder</article-title><source>J Physiol</source><year>1991</year><volume>435</volume><fpage>187</fpage><lpage>205</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1663160</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Griffith</surname><given-names>WH</given-names></name><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Davis</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Whole-cell and single-channel calcium currents in guinea pig basal forebrain neurons</article-title><source>J Neurophysiol</source><year>1994</year><volume>71</volume><fpage>2359</fpage><lpage>2376</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7931521</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hemler</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>VLA proteins in the integrin family: structures, functions, and their role on leukocytes</article-title><source>An